1
00:00:01,044 --> 00:00:03,829
[unsettling foreboding music]

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:06,789
- It appears that village is
indeed amassing military might

3
00:00:06,919 --> 00:00:09,096
and planning something
most dreadful.

4
00:00:09,226 --> 00:00:11,011
- It may be that they're
convincing Flowrem

5
00:00:11,141 --> 00:00:12,882
to stay there just so that
they can use her

6
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,536
as a hostage if they need to.

7
00:00:14,666 --> 00:00:17,104
- We should begin gathering
our troops at once...

8
00:00:17,234 --> 00:00:18,366
Princess!

9
00:00:18,496 --> 00:00:20,759
I understand.

10
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:22,979
We must defeat that village

11
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:26,852
and we have to save Flowrem.

12
00:00:26,983 --> 00:00:30,117
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

13
00:01:56,072 --> 00:02:00,468
[waves lapping]
[minimal pensive music]

14
00:02:07,779 --> 00:02:11,131
[magic humming]

15
00:02:13,002 --> 00:02:15,439
- I'm sorry to bother you
while you're looking busy.

16
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:18,921
- I'm not just looking busy,
I am busy.

17
00:02:19,051 --> 00:02:22,707
I have been put in charge of the
village's accounting practices.

18
00:02:22,838 --> 00:02:26,624
Putting that aside, what brings
you here so late, Father?

19
00:02:26,755 --> 00:02:30,150
- The thing is, our princess
is gathering troops

20
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:32,543
and preparing to go on
a military campaign.

21
00:02:32,674 --> 00:02:34,415
[Flowrem gasping]

22
00:02:34,545 --> 00:02:37,026
- [Flowrem] Our princess
is doing what?

23
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,507
Why would she do
something so absurd?

24
00:02:39,637 --> 00:02:41,987
- While you have been away
from the kingdom,

25
00:02:42,118 --> 00:02:44,990
some have taken the chance to
fill her head with half-truths.

26
00:02:45,121 --> 00:02:46,731
- And by some, you mean.

27
00:02:46,862 --> 00:02:48,516
- The second daughter
of the Gritch family,

28
00:02:48,646 --> 00:02:50,735
the fourth daughter
of the Bugal family,

29
00:02:50,866 --> 00:02:53,085
and the second daughter
of the Mamonrose family.

30
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:56,176
- Aren't those the trio of
politically powerful idiots?

31
00:02:56,306 --> 00:02:59,266
So where exactly are they
planning to attack?

32
00:03:00,789 --> 00:03:01,920
- This very village.

33
00:03:02,051 --> 00:03:03,531
- Huh?

34
00:03:03,661 --> 00:03:05,707
What in the world would
give them such a dumb idea?

35
00:03:05,837 --> 00:03:08,013
I've given them
plenty of reports.

36
00:03:08,144 --> 00:03:10,494
They should know how powerful
this village is.

37
00:03:10,625 --> 00:03:12,279
- I think the reports
were so ridiculous

38
00:03:12,409 --> 00:03:14,324
that they started
to seem unreal.

39
00:03:14,455 --> 00:03:18,285
I tried to have the demon lord
put a stop to this rampage.

40
00:03:18,415 --> 00:03:21,592
But he's far too soft
on his daughter.

41
00:03:21,723 --> 00:03:24,552
- Then do you think it's best
if I convince them to stop?

42
00:03:24,682 --> 00:03:27,642
- They would be
expecting you to do that.

43
00:03:27,772 --> 00:03:29,818
It would cause them to
view you as an enemy

44
00:03:29,948 --> 00:03:31,689
of the Demonic Kingdom.

45
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:34,301
- Then what should I do, Father?

46
00:03:34,431 --> 00:03:37,129
- I just need you to stop their
invasion before it starts.

47
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:39,001
- [Flowrem] When are
they mobilizing?

48
00:03:39,131 --> 00:03:40,045
- Tomorrow.

49
00:03:40,176 --> 00:03:41,221
- Tomorrow?

50
00:03:41,351 --> 00:03:43,266
- Their forces number 300 men.

51
00:03:43,397 --> 00:03:45,877
I was thinking that maybe if
someone from this village

52
00:03:46,008 --> 00:03:49,229
routed their forces,
they'd give up and go home.

53
00:03:49,359 --> 00:03:52,449
- Sure, but if we're careless
about which villagers

54
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,972
find out about this,

55
00:03:54,103 --> 00:03:55,974
it will likely cause
a violent destruction

56
00:03:56,105 --> 00:03:57,193
of the Demonic Kingdom.

57
00:03:57,324 --> 00:03:58,847
- [Beezel] That would
be a problem.

58
00:03:58,977 --> 00:04:02,459
- Hmm, so then, I just need to
show them the difference

59
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:05,897
in military might without
mobilizing the village's forces.

60
00:04:06,028 --> 00:04:10,337
[people shouting indistinctly]
[explosive blasting]

61
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:14,732
[wood breaking]
[people yelling]

62
00:04:14,863 --> 00:04:17,169
- We beg of you,
please, spare our lives!

63
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,954
- [Soldier] Have mercy!

64
00:04:19,607 --> 00:04:21,130
- Hmm?

65
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,044
[people gasping]

66
00:04:22,174 --> 00:04:23,393
Are we done already?

67
00:04:23,524 --> 00:04:24,960
- [Soldiers] Yes.

68
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:26,701
- They're going to give us
ten boxes of apples

69
00:04:26,831 --> 00:04:28,485
just for this?

70
00:04:28,616 --> 00:04:31,793
Do you think maybe we should
punish them just a little more?

71
00:04:34,186 --> 00:04:38,974
- Uh, so who are these girls
standing here frozen solid?

72
00:04:39,104 --> 00:04:40,454
- They're from
the Demonic Kingdom,

73
00:04:40,584 --> 00:04:42,456
and they'd like to
move here.

74
00:04:42,586 --> 00:04:43,848
They've had a change of heart

75
00:04:43,979 --> 00:04:45,241
and are ready to work
themselves to death.

76
00:04:45,372 --> 00:04:46,373
- [Girls] Huh?

77
00:04:46,503 --> 00:04:47,635
- I mean, they're ready to work

78
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:48,940
like their lives depend on it.

79
00:04:49,071 --> 00:04:51,203
- Um, okay.

80
00:04:51,334 --> 00:04:52,683
But even so.

81
00:04:52,814 --> 00:04:54,772
They kind of seem like
they've given up.

82
00:04:54,903 --> 00:04:56,165
Almost like they've accepted

83
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,732
that their lives are over,
or something.

84
00:04:57,862 --> 00:04:59,777
- They'll be fine.

85
00:04:59,908 --> 00:05:02,084
They're all
acquaintances of mine.

86
00:05:02,214 --> 00:05:03,694
So for the time being,

87
00:05:03,825 --> 00:05:06,044
I plan to have them
working for me.

88
00:05:06,175 --> 00:05:08,873
In the event they harm
the village in any way,

89
00:05:09,004 --> 00:05:11,136
please don't hesitate
to dispose of them.

90
00:05:11,267 --> 00:05:12,094
I won't mind.

91
00:05:12,224 --> 00:05:13,530
- That sounded scary.

92
00:05:13,661 --> 00:05:16,446
Great, now that
that's out of the way,

93
00:05:16,577 --> 00:05:18,318
who's that other girl
over there?

94
00:05:18,448 --> 00:05:20,145
- She's here to observe.

95
00:05:20,276 --> 00:05:22,800
I'd like to show her how things
work here in the village.

96
00:05:22,931 --> 00:05:25,368
- My... my name is Yuri.

97
00:05:25,499 --> 00:05:27,631
- Apparently, she was
very worried

98
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:29,241
about my living conditions

99
00:05:29,372 --> 00:05:31,243
here in our village and
wanted to see what it's like.

100
00:05:31,374 --> 00:05:33,898
- You don't need to
give her special treatment.

101
00:05:34,029 --> 00:05:36,771
Please put her to work
knowing she'll be gone soon.

102
00:05:36,901 --> 00:05:39,251
- How does she expect me
to do that?

103
00:05:39,382 --> 00:05:42,037
Great, why don't you
show them around.

104
00:05:42,167 --> 00:05:44,344
- Thank you,
just leave it to me.

105
00:05:45,693 --> 00:05:47,085
Listen up.

106
00:05:47,216 --> 00:05:48,957
If you all put in some
honest work here,

107
00:05:49,087 --> 00:05:51,699
your transgressions against
the village will be forgiven.

108
00:05:51,829 --> 00:05:54,528
That said, in the interest
of keeping this incident

109
00:05:54,658 --> 00:05:56,878
a secret from the rest
of the villagers,

110
00:05:57,008 --> 00:06:00,316
it would be wise not to
divulge your identities.

111
00:06:00,447 --> 00:06:02,449
In other words, Princess.

112
00:06:02,579 --> 00:06:03,624
- Yes, Flowrem?

113
00:06:03,754 --> 00:06:05,887
- You won't get
special treatment.

114
00:06:06,017 --> 00:06:08,455
As long as you're here,
in this village,

115
00:06:08,585 --> 00:06:10,500
you'll just be plain old Yuri.

116
00:06:10,631 --> 00:06:13,677
- That won't be a problem.
[Yuri giggling]

117
00:06:13,808 --> 00:06:17,028
It's been a long time since
I've been called by my name.

118
00:06:17,159 --> 00:06:20,728
- Now then, let's get started
with our tour of the village.

119
00:06:20,858 --> 00:06:22,382
[Flowrem sighing]

120
00:06:23,992 --> 00:06:25,210
[mild carefree music]

121
00:06:25,341 --> 00:06:27,474
- So these fruit are
turned into alcohol?

122
00:06:30,172 --> 00:06:32,479
These plants grow
from inside the water?

123
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,742
[mechanisms warbling]

124
00:06:34,872 --> 00:06:36,831
This contraption
moves not with magic,

125
00:06:36,961 --> 00:06:39,355
but it's powered by
water moving over it?

126
00:06:40,312 --> 00:06:41,444
- [Beastboys] Hello.

127
00:06:41,575 --> 00:06:44,447
- Are you one of the new girls?

128
00:06:44,578 --> 00:06:47,232
- So, Fluffy, look at you.

129
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:49,713
- Hey, that tickles.

130
00:06:49,844 --> 00:06:51,541
- These are apples, right?

131
00:06:51,672 --> 00:06:54,022
I had no idea they
grew on trees like this.

132
00:06:54,152 --> 00:06:55,502
[girls ahhing]

133
00:06:55,632 --> 00:06:58,809
- Oh hey, do we have
some visitors?

134
00:07:00,071 --> 00:07:01,682
- I have never gotten
to eat apples

135
00:07:01,812 --> 00:07:04,293
except for when attending
parties at the castle.

136
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,904
- I ate them every day at home,
never missed a day.

137
00:07:07,035 --> 00:07:08,950
- At my house, we used to
have the merchants

138
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,995
search for them and buy them up
when in short supply.

139
00:07:11,126 --> 00:07:12,823
- [Roaju] So that's
where they went.

140
00:07:12,954 --> 00:07:15,086
- Are those girls that are
with you nobles or something?

141
00:07:15,217 --> 00:07:17,524
- Yeah, yeah,
something like that.

142
00:07:17,654 --> 00:07:19,700
- If we can take over
this village.

143
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:22,311
- It'll be the biggest
money-maker for our kingdom.

144
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:23,660
- [Flowrem] Dispose.

145
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:25,227
- Never mind, forget it,
it's nothing.

146
00:07:25,357 --> 00:07:28,360
[girls giggling]

147
00:07:28,491 --> 00:07:32,364
- Hello there,
I'm Lastismoon of the dragons.

148
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:34,279
Please call me Lasty.

149
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:36,847
- Nice to meet you, Lasty.

150
00:07:36,978 --> 00:07:40,285
She's awfully adorable
for a fierce dragon.

151
00:07:40,416 --> 00:07:42,418
- I know we were
forced to stay out here

152
00:07:42,549 --> 00:07:44,028
but it's gross that
nobles are living

153
00:07:44,159 --> 00:07:46,117
in the middle of
nowhere like this.

154
00:07:46,248 --> 00:07:48,729
- We'll be the laughing stock of
the country when we're back.

155
00:07:48,859 --> 00:07:50,818
- Let's wait for a chance
and escape.

156
00:07:50,948 --> 00:07:52,080
[girls agreeing]

157
00:07:53,908 --> 00:07:55,170
[girls gasping]

158
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,432
[wolves growling]

159
00:07:56,563 --> 00:07:57,955
[girls screaming]

160
00:07:58,086 --> 00:07:59,740
[rooster crowing]

161
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:01,959
[girls whimpering]

162
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:03,134
[air whooshing]

163
00:08:03,265 --> 00:08:04,614
[girls screaming]

164
00:08:04,745 --> 00:08:07,704
[girls whimpering]

165
00:08:07,835 --> 00:08:09,140
- [Flowrem] Have you
learned your lesson?

166
00:08:09,271 --> 00:08:10,054
- [Girls] We have.

167
00:08:10,185 --> 00:08:11,665
- We promise you.

168
00:08:11,795 --> 00:08:13,275
- [Klakkase] We'll work like
our lives depend on it.

169
00:08:13,405 --> 00:08:16,060
- [Rosalind] Just please
don't dispose of us.

170
00:08:16,191 --> 00:08:18,498
- Looks like they're
working really hard.

171
00:08:18,628 --> 00:08:20,674
- They're actually a big help.

172
00:08:20,804 --> 00:08:23,720
Now I can split up the mountain
of office work I had to do.

173
00:08:23,851 --> 00:08:26,027
I'll be happy if I can
keep them working like this

174
00:08:26,157 --> 00:08:28,290
as part of the town hall.

175
00:08:29,639 --> 00:08:32,381
[wolf panting]
[wolf cooing]

176
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:33,948
[Flowrem giggling]
[warm carefree music]

177
00:08:34,078 --> 00:08:36,951
- That's an inferno wolf
your playing with, isn't it?

178
00:08:37,081 --> 00:08:39,649
Is it all right for you to
be petting it like that?

179
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:40,824
- Yeah.

180
00:08:40,955 --> 00:08:42,478
Even though a single
inferno wolf

181
00:08:42,609 --> 00:08:45,089
is said to be dangerous enough
to cause serious damage

182
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,656
and harm to any city it enters,

183
00:08:46,787 --> 00:08:49,572
they're really cute
when they're like this.

184
00:08:49,703 --> 00:08:52,444
- [Yuri] I'm supposed
to throw this?

185
00:08:52,575 --> 00:08:54,316
- [Flowrem] Yeah, they love it.

186
00:08:55,056 --> 00:08:56,231
- Let's see.

187
00:08:56,361 --> 00:08:57,275
Go!

188
00:08:57,406 --> 00:08:58,973
[wolf barking]

189
00:09:00,148 --> 00:09:01,628
[wolves barking]

190
00:09:01,758 --> 00:09:03,151
I could get use to this.

191
00:09:03,281 --> 00:09:06,328
- Eventually.

192
00:09:06,458 --> 00:09:10,462
- This village has been nothing
but wonderful surprises.

193
00:09:10,593 --> 00:09:12,900
I can't believe a world
like this exists

194
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:14,641
outside of the Kingdom.

195
00:09:14,771 --> 00:09:17,513
- I'm pretty sure this is
a very rare exception.

196
00:09:17,644 --> 00:09:21,691
- No, I was just very ignorant
of the outside world.

197
00:09:21,822 --> 00:09:23,998
I tried to bring
war and conflict

198
00:09:24,128 --> 00:09:27,436
to such a wonderfully peaceful
and tranquil village.

199
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,873
- Anyone who intends to do harm

200
00:09:30,004 --> 00:09:31,919
will find themselves on
the receiving end

201
00:09:32,049 --> 00:09:33,747
of a dragon's fire breath.

202
00:09:33,877 --> 00:09:35,966
- And indeed they should.

203
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:37,664
To be honest,

204
00:09:37,794 --> 00:09:40,101
I thought the intel about
dragons living in this village

205
00:09:40,231 --> 00:09:42,843
was a lie meant to deceive
the Demonic Kingdom.

206
00:09:42,973 --> 00:09:44,932
- I warned everyone
on the council

207
00:09:45,062 --> 00:09:47,325
not to get involved
with this village.

208
00:09:47,456 --> 00:09:50,241
The demon lord should've
warned you against it as well.

209
00:09:50,372 --> 00:09:51,808
So why did you do it?

210
00:09:51,939 --> 00:09:55,290
- Honestly, it's your fault.

211
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,205
[Flowrem gasping]

212
00:09:57,335 --> 00:10:00,643
Flowrem, you vanished from the
Demonic Kingdom without warning!

213
00:10:00,774 --> 00:10:03,254
I heard that you had
become a hostage.

214
00:10:03,385 --> 00:10:05,953
I was deeply worried
about you.

215
00:10:06,867 --> 00:10:07,737
- I'm honored, Prin-

216
00:10:07,868 --> 00:10:09,609
- My name is Yuri!

217
00:10:09,739 --> 00:10:11,045
Stop acting subserviant,

218
00:10:11,175 --> 00:10:13,438
we've been friends
since childhood!

219
00:10:13,569 --> 00:10:15,005
You stopped asking me for help,

220
00:10:15,136 --> 00:10:16,485
and then before I knew it,
everything was

221
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,269
princess this and
princess that.

222
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,836
Like I was a stranger.

223
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:21,490
- I'm sorry, Yuri.

224
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:24,624
I'll keep you in the loop
from now on.

225
00:10:25,886 --> 00:10:27,365
- I know, Flowrem.

226
00:10:27,496 --> 00:10:29,324
- Yeah.

227
00:10:29,454 --> 00:10:31,152
Now, let's head back.

228
00:10:31,282 --> 00:10:33,415
It's almost time
for us to eat.

229
00:10:33,545 --> 00:10:34,764
- Okay.

230
00:10:35,547 --> 00:10:36,723
[girls sighing]

231
00:10:36,853 --> 00:10:38,550
- This office work
is really hard

232
00:10:38,681 --> 00:10:40,335
but the food here is great.

233
00:10:40,465 --> 00:10:43,033
- We don't have to worry about
any stressful politics.

234
00:10:43,164 --> 00:10:44,513
We can just relax here.

235
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:46,820
- The baths really heal my soul.

236
00:10:46,950 --> 00:10:48,648
[girls giggling]

237
00:10:48,778 --> 00:10:51,302
- I was worried that they might
have trouble adjusting.

238
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,783
- Seems they've already
fully adapted.

239
00:10:53,914 --> 00:10:55,872
- Are these three
the new girls?

240
00:10:56,003 --> 00:10:57,918
- Yeah. Huh?

241
00:10:58,048 --> 00:11:00,616
You've been at that height
all day, haven't you?

242
00:11:00,747 --> 00:11:02,662
- Yeah, my transformation magic

243
00:11:02,792 --> 00:11:04,925
hasn't really been
working lately.

244
00:11:05,055 --> 00:11:07,449
Oh well, I'm sure
it'll get better.

245
00:11:07,579 --> 00:11:09,364
- I see then.

246
00:11:09,494 --> 00:11:10,539
- [Hiraku] Farming Life...

247
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,019
- [Girls] In another...

248
00:11:12,149 --> 00:11:13,803
- [Hiraku] World.

249
00:11:14,717 --> 00:11:16,240
[stream babbling]

250
00:11:16,371 --> 00:11:17,938
- Right, I know.

251
00:11:18,068 --> 00:11:19,766
[both gasping]

252
00:11:20,723 --> 00:11:21,811
- Ah.
- Huh?

253
00:11:21,942 --> 00:11:23,813
- [Beastboys] It's Big Sis!

254
00:11:23,944 --> 00:11:25,685
- If you don't mind,
I would like to help out

255
00:11:25,815 --> 00:11:27,295
with the farm work as well.

256
00:11:27,425 --> 00:11:29,819
- She's going to do
manual labor?

257
00:11:29,950 --> 00:11:31,473
- But that's work for commoners.

258
00:11:31,603 --> 00:11:33,301
- Please stop this, Princess.

259
00:11:33,431 --> 00:11:34,563
- [Beastboys] Princess?

260
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:35,607
- Pardon?

261
00:11:35,738 --> 00:11:37,000
Wasn't that a secret?

262
00:11:37,131 --> 00:11:38,349
- [Girls] Forget we said that.

263
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,350
- Disposal.

264
00:11:39,481 --> 00:11:41,004
[girls whimpering]

265
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:43,485
- Now then, I want you all
to join me and help out.

266
00:11:43,615 --> 00:11:45,226
- Huh? But we.

267
00:11:45,356 --> 00:11:48,229
- Our specialty is office work
not hard manual labor.

268
00:11:48,359 --> 00:11:50,622
- Don't worry,
we'll show you how.

269
00:11:50,753 --> 00:11:53,060
- [Girls] Ugh.

270
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:55,932
[peaceful cheerful music]

271
00:12:13,994 --> 00:12:15,212
- I learned a lot from you all

272
00:12:15,343 --> 00:12:17,519
during my time
here in this village.

273
00:12:17,649 --> 00:12:19,521
I'm grateful to you all.

274
00:12:19,651 --> 00:12:21,262
- [Beastboy]
You're leaving already?

275
00:12:21,392 --> 00:12:24,961
- I'm sorry. I promise to
come visit you often.

276
00:12:25,092 --> 00:12:28,138
- Uh.
- Um, here.

277
00:12:28,269 --> 00:12:29,357
- [Yuri] Oh my.

278
00:12:29,487 --> 00:12:30,532
- [Sena] They're made
from the wheat

279
00:12:30,662 --> 00:12:32,099
that we harvested together.

280
00:12:32,229 --> 00:12:34,405
- Thank you all so very much.

281
00:12:36,233 --> 00:12:37,365
Flowrem.

282
00:12:37,495 --> 00:12:39,541
Don't forget to come visit.

283
00:12:39,671 --> 00:12:41,151
- Of course.

284
00:12:41,282 --> 00:12:43,501
- [Yuri] Thank you too
for your hospitality, mayor.

285
00:12:43,632 --> 00:12:46,026
- Sure, travel safe.

286
00:12:47,854 --> 00:12:49,290
- Oh, by the way,

287
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,335
are you all not
coming home with me?

288
00:12:51,466 --> 00:12:52,684
[bell dinging]

289
00:12:52,815 --> 00:12:54,208
- There are still
so many great things

290
00:12:54,338 --> 00:12:56,340
left for us to learn
within this village.

291
00:12:56,471 --> 00:12:58,690
- And there's still a ton
of work left to do.

292
00:12:58,821 --> 00:13:00,954
- We haven't repayed
everyone's kindness.

293
00:13:01,084 --> 00:13:03,391
- Therefore, we must stay.

294
00:13:03,521 --> 00:13:06,176
- [Yuri] Could you please stop
eating while you're talking.

295
00:13:06,307 --> 00:13:07,787
- We should leave now.

296
00:13:07,917 --> 00:13:09,136
- Right.

297
00:13:09,266 --> 00:13:11,486
Everyone, I'll see you again.

298
00:13:11,616 --> 00:13:13,880
[magic warbling]

299
00:13:15,316 --> 00:13:17,274
- Looks like she
enjoyed her time here.

300
00:13:17,405 --> 00:13:18,754
- Indeed.

301
00:13:22,236 --> 00:13:23,759
- [Galgardo] Hey, Beezel.

302
00:13:23,890 --> 00:13:25,456
- [Beezel] Yes.

303
00:13:25,587 --> 00:13:28,764
- It's about Yuri, ever since
she returned to the castle,

304
00:13:28,895 --> 00:13:30,810
she's seems a bit
different somehow.

305
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:32,637
- Yes.
- It's like she's grown

306
00:13:32,768 --> 00:13:34,596
dignified all of a sudden.

307
00:13:34,726 --> 00:13:36,598
She looks so busy now.

308
00:13:36,728 --> 00:13:38,774
Even if I try to have
a conversation,

309
00:13:38,905 --> 00:13:40,384
she doesn't make the time.

310
00:13:40,515 --> 00:13:42,169
- It seems that
the princess will begin

311
00:13:42,299 --> 00:13:45,781
to take an interest in politics
and diplomacy pretty soon.

312
00:13:45,912 --> 00:13:48,044
Daughters tend to
grow into adults

313
00:13:48,175 --> 00:13:51,091
before their parents
realize it.

314
00:13:51,221 --> 00:13:52,614
- An adult?

315
00:13:52,744 --> 00:13:54,746
Don't tell me...
she's met a man!

316
00:13:54,877 --> 00:13:55,486
[menacing music]

317
00:13:55,617 --> 00:13:56,748
Who is he?

318
00:13:56,879 --> 00:13:58,272
I, the great
demon lord Galgardo

319
00:13:58,402 --> 00:14:00,927
will tear him apart with
my bare hands myself.

320
00:14:01,057 --> 00:14:03,059
- That possessive attitude
is going to make her

321
00:14:03,190 --> 00:14:04,452
hate you one day.

322
00:14:04,582 --> 00:14:05,845
- She'll hate me?

323
00:14:05,975 --> 00:14:07,324
[Galgardo growling]

324
00:14:07,455 --> 00:14:09,196
- More importantly,
it's time for a meeting.

325
00:14:09,326 --> 00:14:12,503
Let's go and show her what
a cool father you can be.

326
00:14:12,634 --> 00:14:14,549
- Okay, I get it.

327
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:16,943
Leave it to me.

328
00:14:17,073 --> 00:14:19,032
- [Hiraku] A short while
after Yuri left,

329
00:14:19,162 --> 00:14:21,382
we began our pre-winter
crop harvest

330
00:14:21,512 --> 00:14:23,558
and this was the result.

331
00:14:24,776 --> 00:14:26,691
When did all of this happen?

332
00:14:26,822 --> 00:14:28,519
- [Tia] We harvested so much,

333
00:14:28,650 --> 00:14:32,001
this is what we couldn't
fit into storage.

334
00:14:32,132 --> 00:14:33,655
- I'm glad we had
a good harvest.

335
00:14:33,785 --> 00:14:35,483
- But this is more
than we thought.

336
00:14:35,613 --> 00:14:37,964
- In that case, would it
be all right with you

337
00:14:38,094 --> 00:14:39,966
if I sent some of it
to my father?

338
00:14:40,096 --> 00:14:41,532
- Yeah, let's do it.

339
00:14:41,663 --> 00:14:43,883
- Oh then, can we send
some to mine?

340
00:14:44,013 --> 00:14:47,364
- That's fine by me, but who
are your parents anyway?

341
00:14:47,495 --> 00:14:49,018
- [Lastismoon]
From my perspective,

342
00:14:49,149 --> 00:14:50,933
they're Granddad and Grandmom.

343
00:14:51,064 --> 00:14:52,761
- My father lives in
the northern continent

344
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,676
while my mother
lives in the south,

345
00:14:54,806 --> 00:14:57,374
so I'm afraid it's going to be
a bit out of the way.

346
00:14:57,505 --> 00:14:59,594
- There are dragons
north and south?

347
00:14:59,724 --> 00:15:01,683
If that's true then you
must be referring to

348
00:15:01,813 --> 00:15:03,163
the Emperor Dragon Doze,

349
00:15:03,293 --> 00:15:05,556
and the the Hurricane
Dragon Raimaylen

350
00:15:05,687 --> 00:15:07,297
- You're exaggerating!

351
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:09,256
Is that really
what you call them?

352
00:15:09,386 --> 00:15:12,781
- I never knew the dragons
were all connected like this.

353
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,436
- Those are some
pretty intense names.

354
00:15:15,566 --> 00:15:17,655
First, Lasty
stopped by Dryme's

355
00:15:17,786 --> 00:15:19,353
and dropped off the food
we were sharing.

356
00:15:19,483 --> 00:15:21,311
Then she continued
to Shashato City

357
00:15:21,442 --> 00:15:23,748
to drop off their
share of crops.

358
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:26,838
Apparently, Michael asked her
to exterminate a monster

359
00:15:26,969 --> 00:15:28,928
that had been attacking
the trade vessels.

360
00:15:29,058 --> 00:15:29,754
- Sure thing.

361
00:15:29,885 --> 00:15:32,148
You're mine!

362
00:15:32,279 --> 00:15:34,455
[explosive blasting]

363
00:15:34,585 --> 00:15:36,457
Guess what? I got to
take some meat home

364
00:15:36,587 --> 00:15:38,372
as thanks for
killing that thing.

365
00:15:38,502 --> 00:15:40,287
This is definitely
that chanco stuff

366
00:15:40,417 --> 00:15:41,766
you were talking about, mayor.

367
00:15:41,897 --> 00:15:44,508
That means we're having
chanco hotpot tonight.

368
00:15:44,639 --> 00:15:47,642
- Uh, yeah.

369
00:15:47,772 --> 00:15:49,949
Meanwhile, Hakuren headed north.

370
00:15:52,081 --> 00:15:53,865
On her way back,
she found some people

371
00:15:53,996 --> 00:15:55,519
that wanted to
move to our village.

372
00:15:55,650 --> 00:15:58,044
- I'm Ya, the leader of
this group.

373
00:15:58,174 --> 00:16:00,611
- Are you dark elves?
- What?

374
00:16:00,742 --> 00:16:03,658
No, that's not what we are,
we're known as mountain elves.

375
00:16:03,788 --> 00:16:05,921
- Uh, sorry, my mistake.

376
00:16:06,052 --> 00:16:07,531
Please forget about it.

377
00:16:07,662 --> 00:16:09,055
- They can all use fire,

378
00:16:09,185 --> 00:16:12,188
and they're also meat eaters,
like my elven clan.

379
00:16:12,319 --> 00:16:13,755
- So I see.

380
00:16:13,885 --> 00:16:16,279
- Normally, all of us
live up in the mountains,

381
00:16:16,410 --> 00:16:20,196
but as of late, it's become
harder for us to find food.

382
00:16:20,327 --> 00:16:22,894
- They seemed like they were
having some trouble...

383
00:16:23,025 --> 00:16:25,854
so I thought it might be
easier if they lived here.

384
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,899
- I see.

385
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:29,510
Hmm...

386
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,468
What should we do?

387
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:33,427
- I do understand

388
00:16:33,557 --> 00:16:35,995
that no one has the leeway
to help strangers.

389
00:16:36,125 --> 00:16:38,998
If we're causing you trouble,
we'll leave right away.

390
00:16:40,086 --> 00:16:41,565
- No, that's not what I meant.

391
00:16:41,696 --> 00:16:42,871
- Huh?

392
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:45,265
- I was trying to
think of a plan.

393
00:16:45,395 --> 00:16:47,093
We need to figure out
where you'll sleep...

394
00:16:47,223 --> 00:16:49,138
until we can
build you a house.

395
00:16:49,269 --> 00:16:51,836
I was thinking on who
I'll need to talk to first.

396
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:53,838
- So then?
- Yeah.

397
00:16:53,969 --> 00:16:56,841
If you're okay with
living here with us.

398
00:16:56,972 --> 00:16:58,452
[Ya shrieking]

399
00:16:58,582 --> 00:17:00,367
- Thank you so much!

400
00:17:00,497 --> 00:17:03,152
And don't worry, we're fine
sleeping on the ground here.

401
00:17:03,283 --> 00:17:05,241
- [Hiraku] No,
we can't have that.

402
00:17:05,372 --> 00:17:07,722
And so, the group of
mountain elves

403
00:17:07,852 --> 00:17:09,941
became residents
of our village.

404
00:17:10,072 --> 00:17:13,032
- At the very least,
we'll go catch food on our own.

405
00:17:13,162 --> 00:17:15,208
We're excellent hunters.

406
00:17:15,338 --> 00:17:16,774
[lively cheerful music]

407
00:17:16,905 --> 00:17:18,994
[Ya yelling]

408
00:17:20,387 --> 00:17:22,302
[Ya screaming]

409
00:17:22,432 --> 00:17:25,870
Uh, I'm terribly sorry
we couldn't be of more use.

410
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:27,698
- Are you okay?

411
00:17:27,829 --> 00:17:30,223
- [Ya] Is there something
wrong with this forest?

412
00:17:30,353 --> 00:17:31,746
- You think so, too?

413
00:17:31,876 --> 00:17:33,704
Don't hurt yourselves
if its too much.

414
00:17:33,835 --> 00:17:36,620
- That's very
thoughtful of you, mayor.

415
00:17:38,405 --> 00:17:40,407
What's that you're working on?

416
00:17:40,885 --> 00:17:42,061
- Uh.

417
00:17:43,758 --> 00:17:45,977
I was hoping we could
make some pottery here.

418
00:17:46,108 --> 00:17:47,457
- Interesting.

419
00:17:47,588 --> 00:17:50,808
- And now, we bake it
after it's all dry.

420
00:17:50,939 --> 00:17:52,201
- Oh.

421
00:17:52,332 --> 00:17:54,986
[deflated warbling]

422
00:17:55,944 --> 00:17:57,206
What happened to it?

423
00:17:57,337 --> 00:17:59,600
- I guess the soil here
just won't work.

424
00:17:59,730 --> 00:18:02,168
We'll have to go look around
for clay somewhere.

425
00:18:02,298 --> 00:18:05,606
- Please, mayor, would you allow
me the honor of finding that?

426
00:18:05,736 --> 00:18:07,564
We come from the mountains,
and as such,

427
00:18:07,695 --> 00:18:10,306
we understand the earth and
what all lies within it.

428
00:18:10,437 --> 00:18:11,655
- I see.

429
00:18:11,786 --> 00:18:13,918
Isn't it dangerous to
search the area?

430
00:18:14,049 --> 00:18:16,878
- As long as I don't have to
fight, I should be all right.

431
00:18:17,008 --> 00:18:19,315
I'm confident in
my ability to flee.

432
00:18:19,446 --> 00:18:21,709
- Just promise me
you'll be careful.

433
00:18:22,971 --> 00:18:24,233
Wow!

434
00:18:24,364 --> 00:18:26,322
This is great, it's perfect!

435
00:18:26,453 --> 00:18:27,758
- [Ya] I did my best.

436
00:18:27,889 --> 00:18:29,456
- [Hiraku] I wonder if
we can make cups,

437
00:18:29,586 --> 00:18:30,587
and plates, and stuff.

438
00:18:30,718 --> 00:18:32,023
- Of course!

439
00:18:32,154 --> 00:18:33,590
Just leave it to me.

440
00:18:33,721 --> 00:18:34,983
[air whipping]

441
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:37,203
- [Hiraku] They found
another dungeon?

442
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:40,989
- Yes, it's a different one
than where the lamia live.

443
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,078
Ya was able to find the entrance

444
00:18:43,209 --> 00:18:45,472
to the dungeon up north
near the mountains.

445
00:18:45,602 --> 00:18:48,910
I'd like your permission
to send a survey party.

446
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,781
- What if it's dangerous?

447
00:18:50,912 --> 00:18:53,871
- That's one reason we need to
survey the area and learn more.

448
00:18:54,002 --> 00:18:55,438
- I see then.

449
00:18:55,569 --> 00:19:00,139
Well, just don't do
anything too drastic.

450
00:19:00,269 --> 00:19:02,010
- All right, we're
gonna head out now.

451
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,100
- While the survey team was
off investigating the dungeon,

452
00:19:05,231 --> 00:19:08,451
the men's bathhouse
was finally finished.

453
00:19:08,582 --> 00:19:09,931
[Hiraku exhaling]

454
00:19:10,061 --> 00:19:11,846
The dwarves and
the lizardmen can use it,

455
00:19:11,976 --> 00:19:13,848
and so can Dryme
when he visits.

456
00:19:13,978 --> 00:19:17,417
So I definitely didn't build
this just so I could have it.

457
00:19:17,547 --> 00:19:18,940
Yep.

458
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:21,682
[Beastboys laughing]
[water splashing]

459
00:19:22,944 --> 00:19:25,425
Well, I don't mind
how lively it is here.

460
00:19:25,555 --> 00:19:28,863
Remember, you need to
make sure to wash yourselves

461
00:19:28,993 --> 00:19:30,256
before getting in here.

462
00:19:30,386 --> 00:19:31,866
- [Beastboys] Okay.

463
00:19:31,996 --> 00:19:33,563
[startling music]
- Just what exactly do you three

464
00:19:33,694 --> 00:19:35,086
think you're doing out here?

465
00:19:35,217 --> 00:19:37,480
- We... thought this was
the women's bathhouse.

466
00:19:37,611 --> 00:19:40,483
- I won't get mad, so just
tell me the truth, okay?

467
00:19:40,614 --> 00:19:42,746
- [Rosalind] You're about to get
really mad at us, aren't you?

468
00:19:42,877 --> 00:19:45,053
- Well, um, we were
hoping that maybe

469
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:47,055
we could wash the
mayor's back for him?

470
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,884
- We thought it could be a good
chance to get closer to him.

471
00:19:50,580 --> 00:19:51,973
- Listen up.

472
00:19:52,103 --> 00:19:53,714
We're the absolute
lowest-ranking members

473
00:19:53,844 --> 00:19:55,019
in this village.

474
00:19:55,150 --> 00:19:56,978
- What did I say? Bad idea.

475
00:19:57,108 --> 00:19:58,849
- I tried to stop this.

476
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,416
- Huh, what, seriously?

477
00:20:00,547 --> 00:20:02,113
- You know what'll happen
if you try that again.

478
00:20:02,244 --> 00:20:04,290
- [Roaju] Please, don't let
them dispose of us.

479
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:06,988
- [Flowrem] Last warning.
- Huh?

480
00:20:07,118 --> 00:20:10,731
Before long, the dungeon
survey party had returned.

481
00:20:10,861 --> 00:20:12,254
You're all here.

482
00:20:12,385 --> 00:20:13,734
What is it then?

483
00:20:13,864 --> 00:20:15,692
- We should send an
extermination party

484
00:20:15,823 --> 00:20:17,216
to the dungeon up north.

485
00:20:17,346 --> 00:20:18,869
- Something there a problem?

486
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,655
- We confirmed the presence
of a blood viper inside.

487
00:20:21,785 --> 00:20:23,222
[unsettling music]

488
00:20:23,352 --> 00:20:25,354
- Oh, that was the thing
fighting the bear.

489
00:20:25,485 --> 00:20:27,878
- We absolutely
must have its meat.

490
00:20:28,009 --> 00:20:31,055
The survival of our clan depends
on us getting ahold of it.

491
00:20:31,186 --> 00:20:33,667
- Is it really that important?

492
00:20:33,797 --> 00:20:37,061
- Yes, blood viper meat is said
to be extremely valuable.

493
00:20:37,192 --> 00:20:38,889
Eating it fills you
with vitality,

494
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:41,065
improves one's
husband-wife relations,

495
00:20:41,196 --> 00:20:43,329
and is said to even
bless you with children.

496
00:20:43,459 --> 00:20:45,505
[infant crying]

497
00:20:45,635 --> 00:20:47,246
[Ya gasping]

498
00:20:48,551 --> 00:20:50,074
- [Hiraku] Well,
it's almost winter.

499
00:20:50,205 --> 00:20:51,685
Let's talk it over
with the village

500
00:20:51,815 --> 00:20:54,165
before we set out to hunt it.

501
00:20:54,296 --> 00:20:57,256
[mellow music]

502
00:20:57,386 --> 00:21:02,130
And so, autumn faded away
as winter began to approach.

503
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,045
Then one day...

504
00:21:07,091 --> 00:21:08,745
[door creaking]

505
00:21:08,876 --> 00:21:09,877
- Huh?

506
00:21:10,007 --> 00:21:10,965
I never thought I'd see

507
00:21:11,095 --> 00:21:12,836
you of all people bedridden.

508
00:21:12,967 --> 00:21:15,578
What a strange sight
for one to witness.

509
00:21:16,579 --> 00:21:17,928
- Are you okay?

510
00:21:18,059 --> 00:21:19,539
I heard you weren't
feeling well.

511
00:21:19,669 --> 00:21:21,802
- Yeah, I'm fine.

512
00:21:21,932 --> 00:21:23,717
I might have just caught a cold.

513
00:21:23,847 --> 00:21:25,109
- [Tia] Isn't mixing up
different kinds

514
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,024
of medicines your specialty?

515
00:21:27,155 --> 00:21:30,637
- [Lu] I've never tried making a
medicine for myself before this.

516
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:31,942
[Hiraku grunting]

517
00:21:32,073 --> 00:21:33,640
Don't look at me like that.

518
00:21:33,770 --> 00:21:36,643
It's just a bit of nausea
and a slight fever is all.

519
00:21:36,773 --> 00:21:39,646
I'm sure I'll be fine if I rest
for a little while.

520
00:21:39,776 --> 00:21:41,517
- I hope that's all it is.

521
00:21:41,648 --> 00:21:43,258
- This might be a long shot,

522
00:21:43,389 --> 00:21:46,130
but have you found yourself
craving sour foods?

523
00:21:46,261 --> 00:21:48,568
- Uh, now that you mention it,

524
00:21:48,698 --> 00:21:50,352
I don't really have an appetite

525
00:21:50,483 --> 00:21:53,050
but I'm still able to eat
tomatoes and fruits.

526
00:21:53,181 --> 00:21:54,487
- [Tia and Sena] Mm...

527
00:21:54,617 --> 00:21:56,880
- Um, there was someone
in Howling Village

528
00:21:57,011 --> 00:21:58,404
who said the same thing.

529
00:21:58,534 --> 00:21:59,753
- Huh?

530
00:21:59,883 --> 00:22:01,450
- Lulucy, have you
really not figured out

531
00:22:01,581 --> 00:22:02,973
what's happening to you?

532
00:22:03,104 --> 00:22:05,062
- No, what is it?

533
00:22:05,193 --> 00:22:06,499
- That person?

534
00:22:06,629 --> 00:22:07,935
What happened to them?

535
00:22:08,065 --> 00:22:09,197
- Well, um...

536
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:11,852
We congratulated them
on the baby.

537
00:22:12,505 --> 00:22:13,636
- Hmm...

538
00:22:15,377 --> 00:22:17,988
- [Hiraku and Lu] What?!

539
00:22:18,119 --> 00:22:21,427
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

540
00:23:47,208 --> 00:23:50,646
[rustic music playing]

